## 3. GridCycle detail for K♣↔Q♥ (step after the earlier of the two cards)
K♣ = (suit 0, rank 13): its step (Δrow 0, Δcol 13≡0) always targets its own seat -> always overflows
from column c. Q♥ = (1, 12): target (r+1, c-1); if blocked it scans row t from c-1.
Same seat iff (r+1, c-1) is occupied and (t, c-1) is occupied [one cell if t = r+1],
or the scan row is full except one cell (rare). Measured per position i of the card:
 step after K♣: ok=0.246 (earlier card), Q♥-target blocked=1.000, P(t = row+1)=0.467
 step after Q♥: ok=0.246 (earlier card), Q♥-target blocked=1.000, P(t = row+1)=0.473
 model f(i) = phi (q + (1-q) phi), phi = i/51 (fill), q = P(t=row+1); f(51) = 1
 pos   measured ok   model
